<title>USA: Jordan buys 15,000 tonnes optional origin rice.</title>
<headline>Jordan buys 15,000 tonnes optional origin rice.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jordan bought on Tuesday a total of 15,000 tonnes optional origin medium grain camolino milled rice, U.S. exporters and traders said.</p>
<p>The shipment period was slated for September.</p>
<p>The rice was purchased at $419.50 a tonne, cost and freight, Agaba, free out, (sellers pay for cost of unloading) they said.</p>
<p>The rice will be bagged from country of origin, one trader said.</p>
<p>((Doris Frankel 312-983-7305))</p>
</text>
